import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---
<DocsLayout title="Claude Code — Band Docs">
  <h1>Claude Code</h1>
  <p>
    Claude Code is the default coding agent in Band and offers the deepest integration.
    It supports cost tracking, session listing, session resume, user input prompts, and
    skill discovery. Band communicates with Claude Code through the
    <code>@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk</code>, which provides a streaming event
    interface for programmatic control.
  </p>

  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Install the Claude Code CLI by following the official Anthropic documentation at <a href="https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/overview">docs.anthropic.com</a>.</li>
    <li>Authenticate with your Anthropic API key or Claude Pro/Team subscription.</li>
    <li>Verify the installation by running <code>claude --version</code> in your terminal.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>How Band Integrates via Hooks</h2>
  <p>
    Band uses Claude Code's hook system to receive automatic status updates. Band
    installs them into <code>~/.claude/settings.json</code> only when you click Install in the
    banner or in Settings &gt; Agent hooks. These events are registered:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>UserPromptSubmit, PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PostToolUseFailure</strong> — Band marks the worktree as <em>working</em>. <code>PreToolUse</code> for <code>AskUserQuestion</code> or <code>ExitPlanMode</code> marks a <em>question</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>PermissionRequest</strong> — Fires when the agent waits for permission. Band marks a <em>question</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>Stop</strong> — Fires when the agent finishes. Band marks the worktree <em>done</em>, or <em>monitoring</em> while a loop or background task still runs. <strong>StopFailure</strong> marks <em>failed</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>SubagentStart, SubagentStop, PostCompact, SessionEnd</strong> — Keep <em>working</em> while subagents run, end a manual compact and drop the session.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Each hook runs the command <code>band notify</code>, which reads the JSON payload
    from stdin, resolves the worktree from the hook's <code>cwd</code>, and posts a
    status update to the Band server. This is how Band detects agent activity in
    worktrees where Claude Code is running independently (outside of Band-submitted tasks).
  </p>

  <h3>Hooks Configuration</h3>
  <p>
    Band manages hooks automatically. From the dashboard, navigate to
    <strong>Settings</strong> and click <strong>Install Hooks</strong>. Band will locate
    the <code>band</code> CLI binary on your system and write the hook entries into
    <code>~/.claude/settings.json</code>. If you already have other hooks configured,
    Band preserves them and only adds its own entries.
  </p>
  <p>The resulting configuration in <code>settings.json</code> looks like:</p>
  <pre><code set:html={`{
  "hooks": {
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      { "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/bin/band notify" }] }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      { "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/bin/band notify" }] }
    ],
    "PermissionRequest": [
      { "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/bin/band notify" }] }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      { "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/bin/band notify" }] }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      { "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "/usr/local/bin/band notify" }] }
    ]
  }
}`}></code></pre>

  <h2>Session Management</h2>
  <p>
    Claude Code supports full session management through Band. You can:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>View a list of previous sessions for any worktree, including the session summary, first prompt, git branch, and last modified time.</li>
    <li>Resume a previous session by selecting it from the session list. Band passes the session ID to Claude Code, which picks up where it left off.</li>
    <li>Browse the full message history of any session, including user messages, assistant responses, tool calls, and tool results.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cost Tracking</h2>
  <p>
    Claude Code reports the total cost in USD for each session via the
    <code>session-result</code> event. Band displays this in the task completion
    summary, so you can monitor API spend per task. Cost data is available in the task
    history view for completed tasks.
  </p>

  <h2>Configuration Options</h2>
  <p>
    The Claude Code adapter accepts these configuration options through Band's settings:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>model</strong> — Override the default Claude model (e.g., <code>claude-sonnet-4-20250514</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>executablePath</strong> — Path to the Claude Code binary if it is not on your system PATH.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
